            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Smart updates help your device run safely and efficiently. When you turn them on, all future security updates and bug fixes will automatically download when they're available. After an update is downloaded, your device will restart at the time you choose below.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Smart updates help your device run safely and efficiently. When you turn them on, all future security updates and bug fixes will automatically download when they're available. After an update is downloaded, your device will restart at the time you choose below.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏌᏑᏗ ᏗᎪᏢᎯᏐᏗ ᎠᎵᏍᏕᎸᏓ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᎠᏓᎾᏫᏍᏗ ᎤᏓᎵᏏᏅᏓ ᏃᎴ ᎢᏳᎵᏍᏙᏗ ᏂᎦᎵᏍᏗᏍᎬᎩ. ᎢᏳᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎠᎦᏔᎲᏍᏗ ᎢᏯᏂᎢ ᎤᎿᎢ, ᏂᎦᏚ ᎤᏩᎫᏗᏗᏒ ᏧᎾᎦᏎᏍᏗ ᏗᎪᏢᎯᏐᏗ ᏃᎴ ᏍᎪᏯ ᎣᏍᏓ ᏱᏨᏁᏗ ᎠᏎ ᎤᏩᏌᏊ ᏱᎬᏁᎯ ᎡᎳᏗᏟ ᎦᏢᏍᎬᎢ ᎢᏳᏃ ᎾᏍᎩᏛ ᎨᎡᎩ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ. ᎤᎶᏐᏅ Ꭰ ᏗᎪᏢᎯᏌᏅᎯ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎡᎳᏗᎬᏘ ᏫᎦᏢᏅᎯ, ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᎠᏎ ᏥᎭᏂᎩᏍᏓ ᎤᎿᎢ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏟᎵᏒᎢ ᏂᎯ ᏣᏑᏰᏍᏗ ᎡᎳᏗᏨ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="BT ADVANCE FEATURE AVRCP">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>BT ADVANCE FEATURE AVRCP</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>BT ᎠᏓᏌᎳᏙᏗ ᎠᎦᏎᏙᏗ AVRCP</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="NFC services are over the limit size.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>NFC services are over the limit size.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>NFC ᎢᏗᏛᏁᎵᏓᏍᏗ ᏚᎶᏒᏍᏗ Ꮎ ᎠᏎᎸᎢ ᎢᎩᏓ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="In a case the WiFi connection is getting weak or you get out of the WiFi coverage your mobile phone would switch to mobile network.Using WiFi Calling is rated according to the service rates provided by your mobile operator. Details on www.orange.pl/wificalling.Please note that calls to Emergency Numbers eg. 122 will be routed through a mobile network. In case there is no mobile coverage the Emergency Calls could be routed via WiFi Calling service. In such cases your mobile operator may not be able to determine your exact location information and therefore would route your call to the Emergency Centre which is not the closest one for your actual location.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>In a case the WiFi connection is getting weak or you get out of the WiFi coverage your mobile phone would switch to mobile network.Using WiFi Calling is rated according to the service rates provided by your mobile operator. Details on www.orange.pl/wificalling.Please note that calls to Emergency Numbers eg. 122 will be routed through a mobile network. In case there is no mobile coverage the Emergency Calls could be routed via WiFi Calling service. In such cases your mobile operator may not be able to determine your exact location information and therefore would route your call to the Emergency Centre which is not the closest one for your actual location.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎾᎿ Ꭰ ᏗᎪᏪᎵ ᏥᎩ WiFi ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᎩᏍᎬᎢ ᎤᏩᎾᎦᎳᎢ ᏃᎴ ᏂᎯ ᎠᎩᏍᏗ ᎤᎾᏙᏣᎴᏍᏗ ᏥᎩ WiFi ᎫᏢᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᏯᏓᎯᏗᏏ ᎥᎦᏁᏟᏴᏍᎬᎢ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ.ᎬᏗᎭ WiFi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ is ᎠᎦᏈᏴᎡᎲᎢ ᏂᎬᏅ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏥᎩ ᎢᏯᏓᏛᏁᏗ ᏗᎪᏣᎴᏒᏛ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏛ ᎬᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎠᎯᎵᏙᎯ. ᏂᏕᎬᎿᏅᎢ ᎾᎿᎢ www.orange.pl/wificallingᎰᏩᏊ ᎤᏍᏗ ᎪᏪᎸ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᏓᏯᏂ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎤᎵᏍᎨᏛ ᏯᎵᏱᎵᏙᎭ ᏗᏎᏍᏗ eg. 122 ᎠᏎ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎦᏅᎿᏩᏗᏒᎢ ᎠᎦᏛᎴᏍᎩ Ꭰ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ. ᎾᎿ ᏗᎪᏪᎵ ᎤᎿᎢ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎭᏗ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎫᏢᏗ ᏥᎩ ᎤᎵᏍᎨᏛ ᏯᎵᏱᎵᏙᎭ ᏓᏯᏂ ᏰᎵᏊ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎦᎶᎯᏍᏗ ᎾᎿ ᎢᏗᏨ WiFi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᎢᏯᏓᏛᏁᏗ. ᎾᎿ ᎾᏍᎩᏯ ᏂᏓᎵᏱᎵᏙᎲ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎠᎯᎵᏙᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎥᏝ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏰᎵᏉ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏧᏬᎪᏙᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏙᎳᎩ ᎤᏙᏢᏒᎢ ᎧᏃᎮᏢᏗ ᏃᎴ ᎤᏩᎫᏗᏗᏒ ᏯᏓᎯᏗᏏ ᎦᏅᎿᏩᏗᏒᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏪᏯᎾ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏥᎩ ᎤᎵᏍᎨᏛ ᏯᎵᏱᎵᏙᎭ ᎠᏰᏟ ᏥᎩ ᎥᏝ ᏥᎩ ᎾᎥᏂᎨᏍᏗ ᏌᏇ ᎤᎬᏩᏟ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏙᎯᏳ ᎤᏙᏢᏒᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
