            <termEntry id="You have 1 attempt left">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>You have 1 attempt left</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᎯ ᎤᎭ 1 ᏓᏁᎸᏗᏍᎬᎢ ᎠᎦᏍᎦᏂ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id=" Mobile HotspotMobile Hotspot shares your mobile data with other Wi-Fi capable devices.To connect to your Mobile Hotspot:1.Turn on Wi-Fi on the other devices.2.Select  in the list of available Wi-Fi networks.3.If a password is required, enter the password.To save battery, keep your phone plugged in when using Mobile Hotspot. USB TetheringYou can tether your Android device to your computer with a USB cable, to share your device's Internet connection with your computer. 1. USB tethering works with Windows Vista, Windows 7, and Linux, the USB drivers for tethering may be needed.2. If your device has an SD card or USB storage, you can't mount it on your computer when USB tetheredBluetooth TetheringIf your device has mobile data, you can set it up to share its Internet connection with other devices through Bluetooth. 1. Pair your phone or tablet with the device that you want to have share your Internet connection.2. Set up the other device to get its network connection by Bluetooth. You may need to see the instructions that came with that device. ">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term> Mobile HotspotMobile Hotspot shares your mobile data with other Wi-Fi capable devices.To connect to your Mobile Hotspot:1.Turn on Wi-Fi on the other devices.2.Select  in the list of available Wi-Fi networks.3.If a password is required, enter the password.To save battery, keep your phone plugged in when using Mobile Hotspot. USB TetheringYou can tether your Android device to your computer with a USB cable, to share your device's Internet connection with your computer. 1. USB tethering works with Windows Vista, Windows 7, and Linux, the USB drivers for tethering may be needed.2. If your device has an SD card or USB storage, you can't mount it on your computer when USB tetheredBluetooth TetheringIf your device has mobile data, you can set it up to share its Internet connection with other devices through Bluetooth. 1. Pair your phone or tablet with the device that you want to have share your Internet connection.2. Set up the other device to get its network connection by Bluetooth. You may need to see the instructions that came with that device. </term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎤᏗᏞᎩ ᎤᏓᏓᏢ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎤᏗᏞᎩ ᎤᏓᏓᏢᏗᏣᏯᏙᎯᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎬᏗ ᏐᎢ Wi-Fi ᏰᎵᏉ ᎢᎬᏁᏗ ᏥᏂᏕᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ.ᎾᎿᎢ ᎱᏓᎸᎥᎦ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎤᏗᏞᎩ ᎤᏓᏓᏢt:1.ᎯᏍᏚᎢ Wi-Fi ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᏐᎢ ᏥᏂᏕᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ.2.ᎠᏑᏰᏍᏗ  ᎤᎿ ᏕᎦᏅᏛᎢ ᎥᎿᎢ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ Wi-Fi ᏚᎾᏚᏓᎵ.3.ᎢᏳᏃ ᎠᏍᏚᎢᏍᏙᏗ ᎥᎧᏁᎬᎢ ᎢᏯᏛᏁᏗ, ᎠᏴᏍᏗ ᎠᏍᏚᎢᏍᏙᏗ ᎥᎧᏁᎬᎢ.ᎾᎿᎢ ᎯᏍᏆᏂᎪᏓ ᎠᎾᎦᎵᏍᎩ, ᏣᎮᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎫᏓᎸᏙᏗ ᎢᏳᏃ ᎬᏗᎭ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎤᏗᏞᎩ ᎤᏓᏓᏢ. USB ᏗᎵᎪᏙᏗᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏊ ᏗᎵᎪᏙᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ Android ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᎦᏙᎥᎯᏍᏗ ᎠᏍᏆᏂᎪᏗᏍᎩ ᎬᏗ Ꭰ USB ᏔᎷᎩᏍᎩ ᏍᏕᏱᏛ, ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᏯᏙᏍᏗᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᎠᏏᎳᏕᏫᏒᎢ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎬᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᎦᏙᎥᎯᏍᏗ ᎠᏍᏆᏂᎪᏗᏍᎩ. 1. USB ᏗᎵᎪᏙᏗ ᏚᎸᏫᏍᏓᏁᎲ ᎬᏗ Windows Vista, Windows 7, ᏃᎴ Linux, ᏥᎩ USB ᎠᏱᎴᎦ ᎾᏍᎩᎾ ᏗᎵᎪᏙᏗ ᎡᎵᏊ ᎤᏚᎸᏛ.2. ᎨᎡᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᎤᎭ Ꭰ SD ᏆᎾᏲᏍᏗ ᏃᎴ USB ᎠᏍᏆᏂᎪᏙᏗ, ᏂᎯ ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎤᏌᎯᎸ ᎨᎡᎩ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᎦᏙᎥᎯᏍᏗ ᏗᏍᏆᏂᎪᏗᏍᎩ ᎢᏳᏃ USB ᏗᎵᎪᏙᏗBluetooth ᏗᎵᎪᏙᏗᎨᎡᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᎤᎭ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ, ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᏘᎧᎲᎦᏃ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᏯᏙᏍᏗᎢ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᏏᎳᏕᏫᏒᎢ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎬᏗ ᏐᎢ ᏥᏂᏕᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᎠᎦᏛᎴᏍᎩ Bluetooth. 1. ᏗᎵᎪᏙᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᏃᎴ ᏗᎪᏪᎶᏗᎢ ᎬᏗ ᏥᎩ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᏂᎯ ᎤᏚᎵᎭ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎤᎭ ᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏏᎳᏕᏫᏒᎢ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ.2. ᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎦᎸᎳᏗ ᏥᎩ ᎬᏗ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᎩᏍᏗ ᎾᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎬᏗ Bluetooth. ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏉ ᎤᏚᎸᏓ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᎪᏩᏛᏗ ᏥᎩ ᏗᎾᏓᏕᏲᎲᏍᎦ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᎤᎷᏨᎩ ᎬᏗ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ. </term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
