            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="This is the first time this number called you. If this call was spam, you can block this number and report it.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>This is the first time this number called you. If this call was spam, you can block this number and report it.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎯᎠ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏥᎩ ᎠᎬᏱ ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒ ᎯᎠ ᎠᏎᏍᏗ ᎤᏯᎾᎲ ᏂᎯ. ᎨᎡᎢ ᎯᎠ ᏪᏯᎾ ᎨᏎᎢ ᎤᏲᎢ ᎪᏪᎵ, ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎦᏐᎭᎾᎳ ᎯᎠ ᎠᏎᏍᏗ ᏃᎴ ᎬᏂᎨᏒ ᎢᎬᏁᏗ ᎨᎡᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Show warning every time">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Show warning every time</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᎪᏩᏛᏙᏗ ᎠᏓᏕᏯᏔᎲᏍᎩ ᎢᎬᏂᎢᏛᏉ ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Video calls made over the mobile network use both data and voice minutes. Charges may apply.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Video calls made over the mobile network use both data and voice minutes. Charges may apply.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏓᏯᏂ ᏄᎵᏍᏔᏅ ᎦᏬᎯᎸᏙᏗ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ ᎢᏧᎳᏃ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᏃᎴ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎢᏗᏔᏬᏍᏔᏅᎯ. ᏓᎬᏩᎶᏗᏍᎬ ᏰᎵᏉ ᎲᏓ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="LEARN MORE">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>LEARN MORE</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎤᏥ ᎢᎦᎢ ᎠᏕᎶᏆᏍᏗ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Video calls use your high speed data">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Video calls use your high speed data</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏓᏯᏂ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎦᎸᎳᏗ ᎦᏣᏄᎳ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="We all love to hear that familiar voice at the end of the line, but talking face-to-face is so much better! Here’s what you should know to get your real-time connections going:">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>We all love to hear that familiar voice at the end of the line, but talking face-to-face is so much better! Here’s what you should know to get your real-time connections going:</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎢᏧᎳ ᏂᎦᏓ ᎠᏓᎨᏳᏗ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᏛᎩ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᎤᎩᏌᏛ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎤᎿᎢ ᏥᎩ ᎠᎵᏍᏆᏓ ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏍᏓᏅᏅ, ᎠᏎᏃ ᎦᏬᏂᏍᎬ ᏓᎾᏓᎧᏅ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎤᏣᏘ ᏓᏤᎳ! ᎠᎭᏂ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎦᏙ ᏂᎯ ᎾᎢᏳᏃ ᎢᏣᏅᏖᏍᏗ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᎩᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏙᎯᏳ ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒᎢ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᏓᏰᏏ:</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Real Time Text calling ^1">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Real Time Text calling ^1</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎤᏙᎯᏳ ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒᎢ ᎠᎪᎵᏰᏗ ᏫᏗᎬᏗᏍᎩ ^1</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="\t• To use AT&amp;T Video Call, all parties must have Video Call-capable devices, located in HD Voice coverage, with a rate plan eligible to use Video Call. \t• Each Video Call uses both voice and data. The voice portion of the call counts as voice minutes, and the video portion counts as data under your wireless rate plan. \t• Once you have started a Video Call, it will seamlessly switch to Wi-Fi if your device has access to the Internet through its Wi-Fi connection. To continue a video call on Wi-Fi you must also remain connected to the AT&amp;T wireless network. No voice or data charges apply to Video Call over Wi-Fi. \t• The Video Call icon tells you when you are able to make a video call. Other AT&amp;T subscribers can see if you are capable of receiving video calls. This capability indication may not function with subscribers on other carriers. \t• You can disable AT&amp;T Video Call in Call Settings on your device. \t• For more information and restrictions, visit www.att.com/videocall.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>\t• To use AT&amp;T Video Call, all parties must have Video Call-capable devices, located in HD Voice coverage, with a rate plan eligible to use Video Call. \t• Each Video Call uses both voice and data. The voice portion of the call counts as voice minutes, and the video portion counts as data under your wireless rate plan. \t• Once you have started a Video Call, it will seamlessly switch to Wi-Fi if your device has access to the Internet through its Wi-Fi connection. To continue a video call on Wi-Fi you must also remain connected to the AT&amp;T wireless network. No voice or data charges apply to Video Call over Wi-Fi. \t• The Video Call icon tells you when you are able to make a video call. Other AT&amp;T subscribers can see if you are capable of receiving video calls. This capability indication may not function with subscribers on other carriers. \t• You can disable AT&amp;T Video Call in Call Settings on your device. \t• For more information and restrictions, visit www.att.com/videocall.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>\t• ᎾᎿᎢ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ AT&amp;T ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ, ᏂᎦᏓ ᎤᎾᏓᏡᎨᏍᎬ ᎠᏎ ᎤᎭ ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ-ᏰᎵᏉ ᎢᎬᏁᏗ ᏥᏂᏕᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ, ᎢᎬᎾᏕᏅ ᎾᎿ HD ᎤᏁᎬ ᎫᏝᎢ, ᎬᏗ Ꭰ ᎠᎦᏈᏴᎡᎲᎢ ᏗᎫᎪᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ ᏣᎦᏓᏂᎸᏨᎢ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ. \t• ᎢᏧᎳ ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ ᎢᏧᎳᏃ ᎤᏁᎬ ᏃᎴ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ. ᏥᎩ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎢᎦᏛ ᎤᎿ ᏥᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ ᏗᏎᏍᏗ ᎤᎿᎢ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎢᏗᏔᏬᏍᏔᏅᎯ, ᏃᎴ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᎢᎦᏛ ᏗᏎᏍᏗ ᎤᎿᎢ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎤᏓᏄᏴᏛᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏂᏓᏏᎳᏛ ᎠᎦᏈᏴᎡᎲᎢ ᏗᎫᎪᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ. \t• ᏌᏊᏊ ᏂᎯ ᎤᎭ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᏙᏔᏅᎩ Ꭰ ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ, ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᏎ ᎦᏰᏫᏒ ᎬᎾᎨᏒ ᏂᎨᏒᎾ ᎥᎦᏁᏟᏴᏍᎬᎢ ᎾᎿᎢ Wi-Fi ᎨᎡᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᎤᎭ ᎠᏴᏍᏗ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏏᎳᏕᏫᏒᎢ ᎠᎦᏛᎴᏍᎩ ᎨᎡᎢ Wi-Fi ᎫᏓᎸᎢ. ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᎯᎸᏍᏗ Ꭰ ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ ᎤᎿᎢ Wi-Fi ᏂᎯ ᎤᎭ ᎾᏍᏊ ᎤᎷᎴᎢ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏥᎩ AT&amp;T ᏂᏓᏏᎳᏛ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ. ᎭᏗ ᎤᏁᎬ ᏃᎴ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᏓᎬᏩᎶᏗᏍᎬ ᎲᏓ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ ᎦᏬᎯᎸᏙᏗ Wi-Fi. \t• ᏥᎩ ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ ᎠᎢᎧᏂ ᎤᏂᏃᎮᏗ ᏂᎯ ᎢᏳᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎨᎡᎩ ᏰᎵᏉ ᎢᏯᏛᏁᏗ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎪᏒᏗ Ꭰ ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ. ᏐᎢ AT&amp;T ᏔᏓᏅᎵ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎠᎪᏩᏛᏗ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏂᎯ ᎨᎡᎩ ᏰᎵᏉ ᎢᎬᏁᏗ ᎤᎿ ᎠᎩᏍᎬᎢ ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏓᏯᏂ. ᎯᎠ ᎢᎬᏩᏛᏁᏗ ᏗᎧᏃᎮᏍᎩ ᏰᎴᏯ ᎥᏝ ᏧᎸᏫᏍᏓᏁᏗᏱ ᎬᏗ ᏗᏓᏅᏍᏗ ᎤᎾᎿ ᏐᎢ ᎠᏂᎯᏙᎯ. \t• ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎦᎬᏙᏗ ᏂᎨᏒᎾ AT&amp;T ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ ᎾᎿ ᏪᏯᎾ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎤᎿᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ. \t• ᎤᎬᏩᏟ ᎤᎪᏗᏊ ᎧᏃᎮᏢᏗ ᏃᎴ ᏚᏅᏍᏓᏕᎲ, ᎠᏩᏛᎯᏓᏍᏗ www.att.com/videocall.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Got it">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Got it</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎪᎵᎦ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Select new photo">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Select new photo</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏑᏰᏍᏗ ᎢᏤ ᏗᏓᏥᎶᏍᏔᏅᎢ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Remove photo">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Remove photo</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎯᎲᎾ ᏗᏓᏥᎶᏍᏔᏅᎢ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Enriched calling lets you add a subject, photo, and location to your calls. You can also let your recipient know when a call is important.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Enriched calling lets you add a subject, photo, and location to your calls. You can also let your recipient know when a call is important.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏤᎳᏔᏅ ᏫᏗᎬᏗᏍᎩ ᏩᏂᎩ ᏂᎯ ᏗᎧᏁᏉᏍᏗ Ꭰ ᎧᏃᎮᏗ, ᏗᏟᎶᏍᏔᏅ, ᏃᎴ ᎤᏙᏢᏒᎢ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏓᏯᏂ. ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎾᏍᏊ ᏩᏂᎩ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᎦᏁᏍᎩ ᎤᏔ ᎢᏳᏃ Ꭰ ᏪᏯᎾ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎤᎵᏍᎨᏓ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Real Time Text calling">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Real Time Text calling</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎤᏙᎯᏳ ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒᎢ ᎠᎪᎵᏰᏗ ᏫᏗᎬᏗᏍᎩ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Your PIN can’t be the last 4 digits of your phone number">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Your PIN can’t be the last 4 digits of your phone number</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᏨᎤᎢ PIN ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎨᎡᎩ ᏥᎩ ᎣᏂ 4 ᎠᏎᏍᏗ ᎤᎿ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎠᏎᏍᏗ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Cannot record during a call.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Cannot record during a call.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᏕᎦᏅᏅᏛᎢ ᎾᎯᏳ ᎨᏒ ᏪᏯᎾ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id=" Visual Voicemail:You can play your voicemails in the order of your choice.Your most recent voicemails appear at the top of the list.Premium subscribers have access to voicemail text transcripts. Premium subscribers can alsoreceive voicemails and transcripts of voicemails in their email inbox.Setup:If you’re a first time user, you’ll need to set up your voicemail. This is aneasy 2-step process that involves choosing a PIN and a voicemail greeting. Your default PINis the last 4 digits of your phone number, but you’ll need to change it as part of thesetup.Greetings:You can choose from 3 types of voicemail greetings. These are used to greet your callerswhen they reach your voicemail.Custom Greeting: Allows you to record a personal greetingName Greeting: Allows you to record your nameDefault Greeting: Standard greeting with your phone numberHow to change your PIN and greeting?You can change your PIN and voicemail greeting anytime by going to Settings -&gt;Visual Voicemail.How to see this tutorial later?You can revisit this tutorial anytime by going to Settings &gt; Visual Voicemail.What happens when callers leave a voicemail when you don’t have a data connection?You’ll always be notified when you receive a new voicemail. You can listen to yourvoicemails by tapping the “Voicemail” button in your phone app. Your voicemailswill download automatically when a data connection is restored.Are voicemails downloaded automatically?Voicemails will download automatically when you’re connected to Wi-Fi. Whenyou’re using a mobile network, you can turn on auto download by going toSettings &gt; Visual Voicemail. ">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term> Visual Voicemail:You can play your voicemails in the order of your choice.Your most recent voicemails appear at the top of the list.Premium subscribers have access to voicemail text transcripts. Premium subscribers can alsoreceive voicemails and transcripts of voicemails in their email inbox.Setup:If you’re a first time user, you’ll need to set up your voicemail. This is aneasy 2-step process that involves choosing a PIN and a voicemail greeting. Your default PINis the last 4 digits of your phone number, but you’ll need to change it as part of thesetup.Greetings:You can choose from 3 types of voicemail greetings. These are used to greet your callerswhen they reach your voicemail.Custom Greeting: Allows you to record a personal greetingName Greeting: Allows you to record your nameDefault Greeting: Standard greeting with your phone numberHow to change your PIN and greeting?You can change your PIN and voicemail greeting anytime by going to Settings -&gt;Visual Voicemail.How to see this tutorial later?You can revisit this tutorial anytime by going to Settings &gt; Visual Voicemail.What happens when callers leave a voicemail when you don’t have a data connection?You’ll always be notified when you receive a new voicemail. You can listen to yourvoicemails by tapping the “Voicemail” button in your phone app. Your voicemailswill download automatically when a data connection is restored.Are voicemails downloaded automatically?Voicemails will download automatically when you’re connected to Wi-Fi. Whenyou’re using a mobile network, you can turn on auto download by going toSettings &gt; Visual Voicemail. </term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏓᏟᎶᏍᏛ ᎧᏁᎬ:ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎤᎾᏛᏁᎸᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏓᏅᏍᏗ ᎾᎿ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏑᏰᏍᏗ.ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᎪᏗᏗ ᎾᏞᎬ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎬᏂᎨᏒᎢ ᎤᎿ ᏥᎩ ᏩᎦᎸᎳᏗᏴ ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᏕᎦᏅᏛᎢ.ᏫᏓᏤᏢᎢ ᏔᏓᏅᎵ ᎤᎭ ᎠᏴᏍᏗ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎪᏪᎳᏅᎢ ᎬᏂᎨᏒ ᏂᎬᏅ ᎪᏪᎳᏅᎢ. ᏫᏓᏤᏢᎢ ᏔᏓᏅᎵ ᎤᎭ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎾᏍᏊᎦᏁᏍᏗ ᎤᏁᎬ ᏃᎴ ᎬᏂᎨᏒ ᏂᎬᏅ ᎪᏪᎳᏅᎢ ᎾᎿ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎾᎿ ᎤᎾᏤᎵ ᎠᎾᎦᎵᏍᎩ ᎪᏪᎵ ᏂᎬᏅ ᎧᏁᏌᎢ.ᎦᎧᎲᏍᎬᎢ:ᎾᎿ ᏂᎯ ᎨᎡᎩ Ꭰ ᎢᎬᏱ ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒ ᎬᏗᏍᎩ, ᏂᎯ ᎠᏎ ᎤᏚᎸᏓ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎦᎧᎲᏍᎬᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎧᏁᎬ. ᎯᎠ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᎠᎯᏗᎨᎢ 2-ᎢᏯᎳᏍᎬᏓ ᎠᏂᎯᎵᏒ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᎠᏓᏠᏯᏍᏙᏗ ᎤᏑᏰᎭ Ꭰ PIN ᏃᎴ Ꭰ ᎧᏁᎬ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ. ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏓᏁᏟᏴᏍᏗᏍᎩ PINᎨᎡᎢ ᏥᎩ ᎣᏂ 4 ᎠᏎᏍᏗ ᎾᎿ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎠᏎᏍᏗ, ᎠᏎᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎠᏎ ᎤᏚᎸᏓ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎦᏁᏟᏴᏍᏗ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎤᎿ ᎢᎦᏛᏉ ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩᎦᎧᎲᏍᎬᎢ.ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ:ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᏣᏑᏰᏍᏗ ᏅᏓᏳᏓᎴᏅᎯ 3 ᎢᏧᏍᏗ ᎤᎿ ᎧᏁᎬ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ. ᎯᎠᏃ ᎨᎡᎩ ᎬᏔᏅᎯ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᏓᎵᎮᎵᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏰᎵᏍᎩᎢᏳᏃ ᏧᏄ ᎠᏙᏯᏅᎯᏗᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎧᏁᎬ.ᏄᏍᏛ ᎢᏯᏛᏁᏗ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ: ᏓᎵᏍᎪᎸᏓᏁᎲ ᏂᎯ ᎤᎿᎢ ᏕᎦᏅᏅᏛᎢ Ꭰ ᎤᏩᏌ ᎤᏤᎵ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘᏚᏅᏙᎥ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ: ᏓᎵᏍᎪᎸᏓᏁᎲ ᏂᎯ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏕᎦᏅᏅᏛᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏚᏅᏙᎥᎠᏓᏁᏟᏴᏍᏗᏍᎩ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ: ᎢᎬᏩᏍᏗᎭ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ ᎬᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎠᏎᏍᏗᏰᎵ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎦᏁᏟᏴᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ PIN ᏃᎴ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ?ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎦᏁᏟᏴᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ PIN ᏃᎴ ᎧᏁᎬ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ ᎢᎸᎯᏳ ᎬᏗ ᏓᏰᏏ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ -&gt;ᏓᏟᎶᏍᏛ ᎧᏁᎬ.ᏰᎵ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᎪᏩᏛᏗ ᎯᎠ ᎠᏕᎶᏆᏍᏙᏗ ᎣᏂᏯᎨᏍᏗ?ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎠᎪᎵᏰᏗ ᎯᎠ ᎠᏕᎶᏆᏍᏙᏗ ᎢᎸᎯᏳ ᎬᏗ ᏓᏰᏏ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ &gt; ᏓᏟᎶᏍᏛ ᎧᏁᎬ.ᎦᏙ ᏂᏚᎵᏍᏔᏅ ᎢᏳᏃ ᎠᏰᎵᏍᎩ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᏗ Ꭰ ᎧᏁᎬ ᎢᏳᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎤᎭ Ꭰ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ?ᏂᎯ ᎠᏎ ᏂᎪᎯᎸᎢ ᎨᏒᎩ ᎠᏓᏃᎯᏎᏗ ᎢᏳᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎦᏁᏍᏗ Ꭰ ᏗᏤ ᎧᏁᎬ. ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎭᏛᏓᏍᏓ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢᎧᏁᎬ ᎬᏗ ᎤᏟᏍᏓ ᎭᏐᏅᏍᏓ ᏥᎩ “ᎧᏁᎬ” ᎦᏛᏗ ᎾᎿ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎬᏙᏗ. ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎧᏁᎬᎠᏎ ᎡᎳᏗᏟ ᎦᏢᏍᎬᎢ ᎤᏩᏌᏊ ᏱᎬᏁᎯ ᎢᏳᏃ Ꭰ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎪᏢᎯᏌᏅ.ᎨᎡᎩ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎡᎳᏗᎬᏘ ᏫᎦᏢᏅᎯ ᎤᏩᏌᏊ ᏱᎬᏁᎯ?ᎤᏁᎬ ᎠᏎ ᎡᎳᏗᏟ ᎦᏢᏍᎬᎢ ᎤᏩᏌᏊ ᏱᎬᏁᎯ ᎢᏳᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎨᎡᎩ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎾᎿᎢ Wi-Fi. ᎢᏳᏃᏂᎯ ᎨᎡᎩ ᎬᏗᎭ Ꭰ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ, ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎯᏍᏚᎢ ᎤᏩᏌᏊ ᏱᎬᏁᎯ ᎡᎳᏗᏟ ᎦᏢᏍᎬᎢ ᎬᏗ ᏓᏰᏏ ᎾᎿᎢᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ &gt; ᏓᏟᎶᏍᏛ ᎧᏁᎬ. </term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Got it">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Got it</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎪᎵᎦ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Your PIN can’t have more than 2 repeated numbers (such as 1222, 3331)">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Your PIN can’t have more than 2 repeated numbers (such as 1222, 3331)</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᏨᎤᎢ PIN ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎤᎭ ᎤᎪᏗᏊ ᎡᏍᎦᏉ 2 ᎤᏩᏘᎶᏓ ᏗᏎᏍᏗ (ᏕᎧᏁᎢᏍᏔᏅᎯ 1222, 3331)</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Your PIN can’t have more than 2 consecutive numbers (such as 1235, 4561, 5321)">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Your PIN can’t have more than 2 consecutive numbers (such as 1235, 4561, 5321)</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᏨᎤᎢ PIN ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎤᎭ ᎤᎪᏗᏊ ᎡᏍᎦᏉ 2 ᏂᎪᎯᎸᎢ ᏗᏎᏍᏗ (ᏕᎧᏁᎢᏍᏔᏅᎯ 1235, 4561, 5321)</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
