            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Voicemail is not set up on your account. Please contact Customer Service at and tell them the error code is .">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Voicemail is not set up on your account. Please contact Customer Service at and tell them the error code is .</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎧᏁᎬ ᎾᎿ ᎥᏝ ᏘᎧᎲᎦ ᎤᎿᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏚᏓᎸᏗ. ᎰᏩᏊ ᎠᏟᏃᎮᏙᏗ ᎤᏩᏍᎩ ᎢᏯᏓᏛᏁᏗ ᎤᎿᎢ  ᏃᎴ ᎤᏃᎮᏗ ᎢᏯᏂᎢ ᏓᏓᎴᎬᎢ ᎠᏍᏓᏩᏛᏍᏙᏗ .</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Your free trial has ended and you now have Basic Visual Voicemail.If you have more than 20 messages in your voice mailbox, no new messages can be left for you. But don't worry—all the messages you have now will be saved. Save or delete some messages so you have fewer than 20 to make room for new ones.Or subscribe to Premium to keep your larger inbox.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Your free trial has ended and you now have Basic Visual Voicemail.If you have more than 20 messages in your voice mailbox, no new messages can be left for you. But don't worry—all the messages you have now will be saved. Save or delete some messages so you have fewer than 20 to make room for new ones.Or subscribe to Premium to keep your larger inbox.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏎᏊᎢ ᎠᏓᎪᎵᏰᏍᎬ ᎤᎭ ᎤᎴᏫᏍᏔᏅ ᏃᎴ ᏂᎯ Ꭷ ᎤᎭ ᏂᎬᏩᏍᏛᏊ ᏓᏟᎶᏍᏛ ᎤᏁᎬ.ᎾᎿ ᏂᎯ ᎤᎭ ᎤᏥ ᎢᎦᎢ ᎡᏍᎦᏉ 20 ᏗᎪᎵᏰᏗ ᎾᎿ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎪᏪᎵᎧᏁᏌ, ᎭᏗ ᏗᏤ ᏗᎪᎵᏰᏗ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᎦᏍᎦᏂ ᎤᎬᏩᏟ ᏂᎯ. ᎠᏎᏃ ᏤᏍᏗ ᏱᏤᎵᎯᏍᎨᏍᏗ—ᏂᎦᏓ ᏥᎩ ᏗᎪᎵᏰᏗ ᏂᎯ ᎤᎭ Ꭷ ᎠᏎ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᎵᏏᏅᏔᏅᎢ. ᎭᎵᏏᏅᏓ ᏃᎴ ᎠᏍᎪᎸᏗᏍᏗ ᎢᎦᏓ ᏗᎪᎵᏰᏗ ᏓᏛ ᏂᎯ ᎤᎭ ᎦᏲᎳᎨᏍᏗ ᎡᏍᎦᏉ 20 ᎾᎿᎢ ᎪᏒᏗ ᎧᏅᏑᎸ ᎤᎬᏩᏟ ᏗᏤ ᏌᏇ.ᎠᎴ ᏔᏓᏅᎵ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏓᏤᏢᎢ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᏍᏆᏂᎪᏙᏗᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎡᏉᎯᎨᏍᏙᏗ ᏂᎬᏅ ᎧᏁᏌᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Please enter a password that doesn't have 3 or more repeating digits (e.g. 1111, 1112)">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Please enter a password that doesn't have 3 or more repeating digits (e.g. 1111, 1112)</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎰᏩᏊ ᎠᏴᏍᏗ Ꭰ ᎠᏍᏚᎢᏍᏙᏗ ᎥᎧᏁᎬᎢ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᏝᏍᏗ ᎤᎭ 3 ᏃᎴ ᎤᏥ ᎢᎦᎢ ᎬᏩᎦᏘᎶᏍᏓ ᏗᏎᏍᏗ (e.g. 1111, 1112)</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Mobile data is off">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Mobile data is off</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎠᏍᏚᎭ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Verizon provisioning service needs permission to access some things in your device. Select Permissions in App info to enable them.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Verizon provisioning service needs permission to access some things in your device. Select Permissions in App info to enable them.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>Verizon ᎤᎾᎵᏍᏕᎸᏙᏗ ᎤᎾᏓᏍᏕᎸᏗ ᏗᏓᏥᎶᏍᏗᏍᎩ ᏚᏚᎸᏛᎢ ᎠᏓᎵᏍᎪᎸᏓᏁᎯ ᎠᏴᏍᏗ ᎢᎦᏓ ᏧᏓᎴᏅᏛ ᎤᎾᎢ ᏣᏤᎵ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ. ᎯᏑᏰᎦ "ᎠᎵᏍᎪᎵᏗᏍᎩ" ᏗᎬᏙᏗ ᎣᏃᎮᏎᏱ ᎠᎵᏍᎪᎵᏗᏍᎩ ᎢᏯᏂᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Verizon provisioning service needs permissions to read your device configuration.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Verizon provisioning service needs permissions to read your device configuration.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>Verizoon ᎤᎾᎵᏍᏕᎸᏙᏗ ᎤᎾᏓᏍᏕᎸᏗ ᏗᏓᏥᎶᏍᏗᏍᎩ ᏚᏚᎸᏛᎢ ᎠᏓᎵᏍᎪᎸᏓᏁᎯ ᎠᏴᏍᏗ ᎠᎪᎵᏰᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᏄᏍᏛ ᎪᏢᏒᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Your call will not be able to be completed.In the future if you would like to use Wi-Fi for Voice calling you can go to Call settings menu or Mobile network settings menu to turn it on.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Your call will not be able to be completed.In the future if you would like to use Wi-Fi for Voice calling you can go to Call settings menu or Mobile network settings menu to turn it on.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏪᏯᎾ ᎠᏎ ᎥᏝ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏰᎵ ᎢᏯᏛᏁᏗ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᏍᏆᏙᎾ.ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᎤᏩᎫᏗᏗᏒ ᎾᎿ ᏂᎯ ᏯᏓᎯᏗᏏ ᏣᎸᏉᏛ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ Wi-Fi ᎤᎬᏩᏟ ᎤᏁᎬ ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ Ꭷ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᏫᎬᏙᏗ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎪᏪᎳᎾᎥᎢ ᏃᎴ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎪᏪᎳᎾᎥᎢ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᎦᏔᎲᏍᏗ ᎾᎿ ᎤᎿᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="If you turn off Wi-Fi Calling, all your future calls will go over the mobile network. If the mobile network isn't available, you may not be able to make calls.In the future, if you want to use Wi-Fi for Voice Calling you can turn on Wi-Fi Calling by going to Call settings menu or Mobile network settings menu.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>If you turn off Wi-Fi Calling, all your future calls will go over the mobile network. If the mobile network isn't available, you may not be able to make calls.In the future, if you want to use Wi-Fi for Voice Calling you can turn on Wi-Fi Calling by going to Call settings menu or Mobile network settings menu.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎾᎿ ᏂᎯ ᎠᏍᏚᏗ Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ, ᏂᎦᏓ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏩᎫᏗᏗᏒ ᏓᏯᏂ ᎠᏎ ᎮᎾ ᎢᏴᏛ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ. ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ, ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎥᏝ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏰᎵ ᎢᏯᏛᏁᏗ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎪᏒᏗ ᏓᏯᏂ.ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᎤᏩᎫᏗᏗᏒ ᎾᎿ ᏂᎯ ᎤᏚᎵᎭ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ Wi-Fi ᎤᎬᏩᏟ ᎤᏁᎬ ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎯᏍᏚᎢ Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᎬᏗ ᏓᏰᏏ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᏫᎬᏙᏗ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎪᏪᎳᎾᎥᎢ ᏃᎴ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎪᏪᎳᎾᎥᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Wi-Fi Calling lets you make calls using Wi-Fi when the mobile network is not available.To set up Wi-Fi Calling you will need to enter a US address. This address will be used by emergency services as your location if you make an emergency \(E911\) call over Wi-Fi from this phone within the US.We recommend you change this address when you make calls using a different Wi-Fi network so your location information is accurate. You can change your location any time by going to Wi-Fi Calling in the Call settings menu or Mobile network settings menu.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Wi-Fi Calling lets you make calls using Wi-Fi when the mobile network is not available.To set up Wi-Fi Calling you will need to enter a US address. This address will be used by emergency services as your location if you make an emergency \(E911\) call over Wi-Fi from this phone within the US.We recommend you change this address when you make calls using a different Wi-Fi network so your location information is accurate. You can change your location any time by going to Wi-Fi Calling in the Call settings menu or Mobile network settings menu.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᏗᎵᏍᎪᎸᏔᏅ ᏂᎯ ᎪᏒᏗ ᏓᏯᏂ ᎬᏗᎭ Wi-Fi ᎢᏳᏃ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎥᏝ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ.ᎾᎿᎢ ᎦᎧᎲᏍᎬᎢ Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᏂᎯ ᎠᏎ ᎤᏚᎸᏓ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᏴᏍᏗ Ꭰ US ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ. ᎯᎠ ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ ᎠᏎ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎬᏔᏅᎢ ᎬᏗ ᎤᏟᏍᏓ ᎢᎦᎵᏍᏗᏍᎩ ᎢᏗᏛᏁᎵᏓᏍᏗ ᎤᎿᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏙᏢᏒᎢ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏂᎯ ᎪᏒᏗ Ꭰ ᎤᏟᏍᏓ ᎢᎦᎵᏍᏗᏍᎩ \(E911\) ᏪᏯᎾ ᎢᏴᏛ Wi-Fi ᏅᏓᏳᏓᎴᏅᎯ ᎯᎠ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎠᏫᏂᏗᏢ ᏥᎩ US.ᎠᏴ ᎦᎸᏉᏗᎭ ᏂᎯ ᎯᏁᏟᏴᎾ ᎯᎠ ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ ᎢᏳᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎪᏒᏗ ᏓᏯᏂ ᎬᏗᎭ Ꭰ ᏧᏓᎴᎿᎢ Wi-Fi ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᏓᏛ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏙᏢᏒᎢ ᎧᏃᎮᏢᏗ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏗᏙᎳᎩ. ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎯᏁᏟᏴᎾ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏙᏢᏒᎢ ᎢᎸᎯᏳ ᎬᏗ ᏓᏰᏏ ᎾᎿᎢ Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎪᏪᎳᎾᎥᎢ ᏃᎴ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎪᏪᎳᎾᎥᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Can't access during call.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Can't access during call.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᏩᏴᏍᏗᎢ ᎾᎯᏳ ᏪᏯᎾ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Your phone was rebooted and mobile data connection is turned off. Your phone's Video Calling function won't work when mobile data is off. Also, you won't be able to use the Internet, Email or other apps that need a data connection unless you use Wi-Fi.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Your phone was rebooted and mobile data connection is turned off. Your phone's Video Calling function won't work when mobile data is off. Also, you won't be able to use the Internet, Email or other apps that need a data connection unless you use Wi-Fi.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎨᏎᎢ ᏥᎭᏂᎩᏍᏗ ᏃᎴ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᏍᏚᏅᎢ. ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᏗᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᏧᎸᏫᏍᏓᏁᏗᏱ ᏝᏍᏗ ᏗᎦᎸᏫᏍᏓᏁᏗ ᎢᏳᏃ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᏍᏚᎭ. ᎾᏍᏉ, ᏂᎯ ᏝᏰᏍ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏰᎵᏉ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏏᎳᏕᏫᏒᎢ, ᎠᎾᎦᎵᏍᎩ ᎪᏪᎵ, ᏃᎴ ᏐᎢ ᏗᎬᏙᏗ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᎤᏚᎸᏓ Ꭰ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎢᏳᏍᎩᏂ ᏂᎯ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ Wi-Fi.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Allow data access?">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Allow data access?</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᎵᏍᎪᎸᏙᏗ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎠᏴᏍᏗ?</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Deny data roaming access for this trip">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Deny data roaming access for this trip</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏆᏓᏱᎸᎢ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎡᏙᎵᏙᎲ ᏩᏴᏍᏗᎢ ᎤᎬᏩᏟ ᎯᎠ ᎠᏁᎳᏗᏍᏗ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Your phone's Video Calling function won't work when mobile data is off. Also, you won't be able to use the Internet, Email or other apps that need a data connection unless you use Wi-Fi.Turn off the mobile data connection?">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Your phone's Video Calling function won't work when mobile data is off. Also, you won't be able to use the Internet, Email or other apps that need a data connection unless you use Wi-Fi.Turn off the mobile data connection?</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᏗᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᏧᎸᏫᏍᏓᏁᏗᏱ ᏝᏍᏗ ᏗᎦᎸᏫᏍᏓᏁᏗ ᎢᏳᏃ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᏍᏚᎭ. ᎾᏍᏉ, ᏂᎯ ᏝᏰᏍ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏰᎵᏉ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏏᎳᏕᏫᏒᎢ, ᎠᎾᎦᎵᏍᎩ ᎪᏪᎵ, ᏃᎴ ᏐᎢ ᏗᎬᏙᏗ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᎤᏚᎸᏓ Ꭰ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎢᏳᏍᎩᏂ ᏂᎯ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ Wi-Fi.ᎠᏍᏚᏗ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ?</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Mobile Data Not Available">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Mobile Data Not Available</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎥᏝ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Voice and data roaming">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Voice and data roaming</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎤᏁᎬ ᏃᎴ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎡᏙᎵᏙᎲ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Regular loop">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Regular loop</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎤᏐᏱᎭᏊ ᎤᏓᏕᏍᏗ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Deny data roaming access">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Deny data roaming access</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏆᏓᏱᎸᎢ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎡᏙᎵᏙᎲ ᏩᏴᏍᏗᎢ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Unless you use Wi-Fi, you won't be able to use the Internet, Email or other apps that require a data connection.Turn off the mobile data connection?">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Unless you use Wi-Fi, you won't be able to use the Internet, Email or other apps that require a data connection.Turn off the mobile data connection?</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎢᏳᏍᎩᏂ ᏂᎯ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ Wi-Fi, ᏂᎯ ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎨᏒᎩ ᏰᎵᏉ ᎢᏯᏛᏁᏗ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ ᎠᏏᎳᏕᏫᏒᎢ, ᎠᎾᎦᎵᏍᎩ ᎪᏪᎵ ᏃᎴ ᎬᏗ ᏗᎬᏙᏗ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᎠᏎᏯᏛᏁᏗ a ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ.ᎠᏍᏚᏗ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ?</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id=" seconds">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term> seconds</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term> ᏓᏓᎾᏩᏍᎬ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Connect to data services while roaming">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Connect to data services while roaming</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎱᏓᎸᎥᎦ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎢᏗᏛᏁᎵᏓᏍᏗ ᎢᏳᏃ ᎡᏙᎵᏙᎲ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Your phone was rebooted and mobile data connection is turned off. Unless you use Wi-Fi, you won't be able to use the Internet, Email or other apps that require a data connection.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Your phone was rebooted and mobile data connection is turned off. Unless you use Wi-Fi, you won't be able to use the Internet, Email or other apps that require a data connection.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎨᏎᎢ ᏥᎭᏂᎩᏍᏗ ᏃᎴ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᏍᏚᏅᎢ. ᎢᏳᏍᎩᏂ ᏂᎯ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ Wi-Fi, ᏂᎯ ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎨᏒᎩ ᏰᎵᏉ ᎢᏯᏛᏁᏗ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ ᎠᏏᎳᏕᏫᏒᎢ, ᎠᎾᎦᎵᏍᎩ ᎪᏪᎵ ᏃᎴ ᎬᏗ ᏗᎬᏙᏗ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᎠᏎᏯᏛᏁᏗ a ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Last factory data reset">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Last factory data reset</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎣᏂ ᎤᏃᏢᏅᏗ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎢᎦᎧᎯᎲᏍᏗ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Mobile hotspot unavailable">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Mobile hotspot unavailable</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎬᎯᏓᏍᏗ ᎤᏙᏢᏒᎢ ᎭᏗ ᎬᏙᏗ ᏱᎩ ᎭᏗ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ ᏱᎩ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Your phone will turn off mobile data once it reaches the limit you set.Since data usage is measured by your phone, and your carrier may account for usage differently, consider setting a conservative limit.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Your phone will turn off mobile data once it reaches the limit you set.Since data usage is measured by your phone, and your carrier may account for usage differently, consider setting a conservative limit.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᏨᏅᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎠᏎᎢ ᎠᏍᏚᏗ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎦᏟᏌᏅᎯ ᏌᏊ ᎢᏳᏩᎫᏗ ᎨᏒᎢ ᎠᏙᏯᏅᎯᏗᎠ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏎᎸᎯ ᏂᎯ ᎤᎾᏓᏡᎬ.ᏂᏓᏳᏓᎴᏅᏓ ᎦᏟᏌᏅᎯ ᎬᏗᏍᎬ ᎨᏒᎢ ᎢᏳᏟᎶᏛ ᎬᏗ ᏂᏨᏅᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ, ᎠᎴ ᏂᏨᏅᎢ ᎠᏫᏗᏍᎩ ᏰᎵᏉ ᎠᏚᏓᎸᏗ ᎤᎬᏩᏟ ᎬᏗᏍᎬ ᏧᏓᎴᎿᎢᎭ, ᎭᏓᏅᏛᎵ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ Ꭰ ᏗᎪᎯᏍᏗᏍᎩ ᎨᏎᏍᏗ ᎠᏎᎸᎯ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Data roaming">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Data roaming</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎡᏙᎵᏙᎲ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="To sign up for a global data plan, call global support at 908-559-4899.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>To sign up for a global data plan, call global support at 908-559-4899.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᏖᎳᏗᏍᏗ ᎤᎬᏩᏟ Ꭰ ᎡᎶᎯ ᎢᎬᎾᏕᎾ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᏗᎫᎪᏔᏂᏙᎸᎯ, ᏪᏯᎾ ᎡᎶᎯ ᎢᎬᎾᏕᎾ ᏕᎦᎫᏍᏛᏁᎭ ᎤᎿᎢ 908-559-4899.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Global data roaming access allowed">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Global data roaming access allowed</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎡᎶᎯ ᎢᎬᎾᏕᎾ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎡᏙᎵᏙᎲ ᎠᏴᏍᏗ ᎠᎵᏍᎪᎸᏔᏅ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Couldn't get data from the server (). Please try again later.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Couldn't get data from the server (). Please try again later.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎤᏄᎸᏅᎢ ᎠᎩᏍᏗ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᏅᏓᏳᏓᎴᏅᎯ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏯᏙᎯᎯ (). ᎰᏩᏊ ᏏᏊ ᎪᎯᏴ ᎯᎭᏁᎵᏔᏅᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Allows application to receive and process DM Register SMS messages.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Allows application to receive and process DM Register SMS messages.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏗᏓᎵᏍᎪᎸᏓᏁᎯ ᎾᏍᎩ ᎬᏙᏗ ᎾᎢ ᎤᎩᏍᏒ ᎠᎴ ᎠᏂᎯᎵᏒ DM ᏚᏙᎥ ᎤᏬᏪᎶᏗ SMS ᎨᏥᏃᎯᏎᏗ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Alert me when I've used this amount of mobile data:">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Alert me when I've used this amount of mobile data:</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏗᏍᎩᏃᏎᎸ ᎯᏯ ᎠᎦᏛᏅ ᎨᏍᎡᏍᏗ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎦᏟᏌᏅᎢ:</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Time">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Time</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Can't modify settings.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Can't modify settings.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎤᏃᏒᎯᏐᏗ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Address couldn't be updated">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Address couldn't be updated</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎪᏢᎯᏌᏅ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Can't turn on Wi-Fi Calling during call.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Can't turn on Wi-Fi Calling during call.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎯᏍᏚᎢ Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᎾᎯᏳ ᏪᏯᎾ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Wi-Fi Calling lets you make calls using Wi-Fi when the mobile network is unavailable. To turn it on, confirm or change the U.S. address where you want emergency responders sent if you call 911, and accept the Terms and Conditions below. It is very important that you update your 911 address (which can be done at any time through your device settings) whenever you change your location, since this is the location that will be given to emergency services when you dial 911.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Wi-Fi Calling lets you make calls using Wi-Fi when the mobile network is unavailable. To turn it on, confirm or change the U.S. address where you want emergency responders sent if you call 911, and accept the Terms and Conditions below. It is very important that you update your 911 address (which can be done at any time through your device settings) whenever you change your location, since this is the location that will be given to emergency services when you dial 911.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᏗᎵᏍᎪᎸᏔᏅ ᏂᎯ ᎪᏒᏗ ᏓᏯᏂ ᎬᏗᎭ Wi-Fi ᎢᏳᏃ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎭᏗ ᎬᏙᏗ ᏱᎩ ᎭᏗ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ ᏱᎩ. ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᎦᏔᎲᏍᏗ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎤᎿᎢ, ᏦᎯᏳᏙᏗ ᏃᎴ ᎯᏁᏟᏴᎾ ᏥᎩ U.S. ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ ᎭᏢᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎤᏚᎵᎭ ᎤᏟᏍᏓ ᎢᎦᎵᏍᏗᏍᎩ ᎦᏬᎯᎵᏴᏍᏗ ᏭᏅᏅᎢ ᎾᎿ ᏂᎯ ᏪᏯᎾ 911, ᏃᎴ ᏗᏓᏂᎸᎢᏍᏗ ᏥᎩ ᏗᏓᏁᏤᎸ ᏃᎴ ᏂᏚᏍᏗᏓᏅᎢ ᎡᎳᏗᏨ. ᎾᎿ ᎰᎡᎢ ᎤᏣᏘ ᎤᎵᏍᎨᏓ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᏂᎯ ᏗᎪᏢᎯᏐᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ 911 ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ (ᎢᏳᏍᏗ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᏍᏆᏗᏍᏗ ᎤᎿᎢ ᎢᎸᎯᏳ ᏭᎵᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ) ᎢᏳᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎯᏁᏟᏴᎾ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏙᏢᏒᎢ, ᏥᎨᏒ ᎯᎠ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏥᎩ ᎤᏙᏢᏒᎢ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᎠᏎ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎡᏥᏁᎸᎯ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎤᏟᏍᏓ ᎢᎦᎵᏍᏗᏍᎩ ᎢᏗᏛᏁᎵᏓᏍᏗ ᎢᏳᏃ ᏂᎯ ᏗᏎᏍᏗ ᏗᏐᎥᏍᏗᏍᎩ 911.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="We could not find the address that you entered:">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>We could not find the address that you entered:</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏴ ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎯᏩᏔ ᏥᎩ ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᏂᎯ ᎠᏴᏍᏙᏗ:</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Free Space">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Free Space</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏚᏓᎴᎩ ᎤᏜᏅᏛ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Unable to activate Wi-Fi calling at this time. Please try again later.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Unable to activate Wi-Fi calling at this time. Please try again later.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎤᏓᏄᎸᏅ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎤᏂᎩᏍᏗᏍᎩ Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᎤᎿᎢ ᎯᎠ ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒ. ᎰᏩᏊ ᏏᏊ ᎪᎯᏴ ᎯᎭᏁᎵᏔᏅᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Call not connected">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Call not connected</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏫᎬᏔᏅ ᎭᏗ ᏱᏣᏚᏓᎵ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Unable to activate Wi-Fi calling at this time.Please try again later.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Unable to activate Wi-Fi calling at this time.Please try again later.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎤᏓᏄᎸᏅ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎤᏂᎩᏍᏗᏍᎩ Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᎤᎿᎢ ᎯᎠ ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒ.ᎰᏩᏊ ᏏᏊ ᎪᎯᏴ ᎯᎭᏁᎵᏔᏅᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Can't connect to the network. Please try again later.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Can't connect to the network. Please try again later.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᏗᎵᎪᏙᏗ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ. ᎰᏩᏊ ᏏᏊ ᎪᎯᏴ ᎯᎭᏁᎵᏔᏅᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="We could not find the address that you entered because the street address could not be found, or the city, state, and zip code may not be correct.If your city, state, and zip are not correct tap Edit, otherwise tap Save Anyway.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>We could not find the address that you entered because the street address could not be found, or the city, state, and zip code may not be correct.If your city, state, and zip are not correct tap Edit, otherwise tap Save Anyway.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏴ ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎠᏩᏛᏗ ᏥᎩ ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᏂᎯ ᎠᏴᏍᏙᏗ ᏂᏗᎦᎵᏍᏙᏗᏍᎬᏃ ᏥᎩ ᎦᎳᏅᏛᎢ ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ be ᎠᏩᏛᏓ, ᏃᎴ ᏥᎩ ᎦᏚᎲ, ᎧᏃᎮᏗ, ᏃᎴ ᏫᎦᏅᏗ ᎠᏎᏍᏗ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎥᏝ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏚᏳᎪᏛᎢ.ᎾᎿ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎦᏚᎲ, ᎧᏃᎮᏗ, ᏃᎴ ᎯᎧᏁᎦ ᎨᎡᎩ ᎥᏝ ᏚᏳᎪᏛᎢ ᎤᏟᏍᏓ ᎠᏒᏂᎸ ᎦᏁᏟᏴᏓ ᎪᏪᎸ, ᎢᏳᏃ ᏰᎵ ᎤᏟᏍᏓ ᎠᏒᏂᎸ ᎭᎵᏏᏅᏓ ᏱᏂᎦᎵᏍᏗᏉ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Wi-Fi Calling lets you make calls using Wi-Fi when the mobile network is not available.To set up Wi-Fi Calling you will need to enter a US address. This address will be used by emergency services as your location if you make an emergency \(E911\) call over Wi-Fi from this phone within the US.We recommend you change this address when you make calls using a different Wi-Fi network so your location information is accurate. You can change your location any time by going to Wi-Fi Calling in the Call settings menu.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Wi-Fi Calling lets you make calls using Wi-Fi when the mobile network is not available.To set up Wi-Fi Calling you will need to enter a US address. This address will be used by emergency services as your location if you make an emergency \(E911\) call over Wi-Fi from this phone within the US.We recommend you change this address when you make calls using a different Wi-Fi network so your location information is accurate. You can change your location any time by going to Wi-Fi Calling in the Call settings menu.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᏗᎵᏍᎪᎸᏔᏅ ᏂᎯ ᎪᏒᏗ ᏓᏯᏂ ᎬᏗᎭ Wi-Fi ᎢᏳᏃ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎥᏝ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ.ᎾᎿᎢ ᎦᎧᎲᏍᎬᎢ Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᏂᎯ ᎠᏎ ᎤᏚᎸᏓ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᏴᏍᏗ Ꭰ US ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ. ᎯᎠ ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ ᎠᏎ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎬᏔᏅᎢ ᎬᏗ ᎤᏟᏍᏓ ᎢᎦᎵᏍᏗᏍᎩ ᎢᏗᏛᏁᎵᏓᏍᏗ ᎤᎿᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏙᏢᏒᎢ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏂᎯ ᎪᏒᏗ Ꭰ ᎤᏟᏍᏓ ᎢᎦᎵᏍᏗᏍᎩ \(E911\) ᏪᏯᎾ ᎢᏴᏛ Wi-Fi ᏅᏓᏳᏓᎴᏅᎯ ᎯᎠ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎠᏫᏂᏗᏢ ᏥᎩ US.ᎠᏴ ᎦᎸᏉᏗᎭ ᏂᎯ ᎯᏁᏟᏴᎾ ᎯᎠ ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ ᎢᏳᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎪᏒᏗ ᏓᏯᏂ ᎬᏗᎭ Ꭰ ᏧᏓᎴᎿᎢ Wi-Fi ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᏓᏛ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏙᏢᏒᎢ ᎧᏃᎮᏢᏗ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏗᏙᎳᎩ. ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎯᏁᏟᏴᎾ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏙᏢᏒᎢ ᎢᎸᎯᏳ ᎬᏗ ᏓᏰᏏ ᎾᎿᎢ Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎪᏪᎳᎾᎥᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Can't modify settings during call.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Can't modify settings during call.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎤᏃᏒᎯᏐᏗ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎾᎯᏳ ᏪᏯᎾ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="The address entered could not be validated by Emergency Service Providers.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>The address entered could not be validated by Emergency Service Providers.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏥᎩ ᎪᏪᎵ ᏧᏁᏍᏗᎢ ᎠᏴᏍᏙᏗ ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎪᎯᏳᏙᏗ ᎬᏗ ᎤᏟᏍᏓ ᎢᎦᎵᏍᏗᏍᎩ ᎤᎾᏓᏍᏕᎸᏗ ᏓᎾᏓᏁᏢᏍᎬᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Don't remind me again">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Don't remind me again</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏤᏍᏗ ᎠᏓᏅᏓᏗᏍᏙᏗ ᎠᏯ ᏏᏊ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Call transferring">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Call transferring</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏪᏯᎾ ᏗᎲᏍᏗᏱ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="If you turn off Wi-Fi Calling, all your future calls will go over the mobile network. If the mobile network isn't available, you may not be able to make calls.In the future, if you want to use Wi-Fi for Voice Calling you can turn on Wi-Fi Calling by going to Call settings menu.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>If you turn off Wi-Fi Calling, all your future calls will go over the mobile network. If the mobile network isn't available, you may not be able to make calls.In the future, if you want to use Wi-Fi for Voice Calling you can turn on Wi-Fi Calling by going to Call settings menu.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎾᎿ ᏂᎯ ᎠᏍᏚᏗ Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ, ᏂᎦᏓ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏩᎫᏗᏗᏒ ᏓᏯᏂ ᎠᏎ ᎮᎾ ᎢᏴᏛ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ. ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ, ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎥᏝ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏰᎵ ᎢᏯᏛᏁᏗ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎪᏒᏗ ᏓᏯᏂ.ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᎤᏩᎫᏗᏗᏒ ᎾᎿ ᏂᎯ ᎤᏚᎵᎭ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ Wi-Fi ᎤᎬᏩᏟ ᎤᏁᎬ ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎯᏍᏚᎢ Wi-Fi ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᎬᏗ ᏓᏰᏏ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᏫᎬᏙᏗ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ ᎪᏪᎳᎾᎥᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="You are currently out of range of the mobile network.Would you like to use Wi-Fi to make and receive voice calls when the mobile network is not available?">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>You are currently out of range of the mobile network.Would you like to use Wi-Fi to make and receive voice calls when the mobile network is not available?</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᎯ ᎨᎡᎩ ᏃᏊᎨᏒᎢ ᎦᏅᎪᏫᏛ ᎾᎿ ᎢᎬᎾᏕᎾ ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ.ᏯᏓᎯᏗᏏ ᏂᎯ ᎢᏳᏍᏘ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎬᏔᏂᏓᏍᏗ Wi-Fi ᎾᎿᎢ ᎪᏒᏗ ᏃᎴ ᎦᏁᏍᏗ ᎤᏁᎬ ᏓᏯᏂ ᎢᏳᏃ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᏧᎾᏚᏓᎵ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎥᏝ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ?</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Requesting SIM service provider unlock\u2026">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Requesting SIM service provider unlock\u2026</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏔᏲᎯᏍᏗ SIM ᎢᏯᏓᏛᏁᏗ ᎠᏓᏁᎸᏍᎩ ᎦᏐᎭᎾᎳᎩᏍᏗ\u2026</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="SIM Service Provider unlock request unsuccessful.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>SIM Service Provider unlock request unsuccessful.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>SIM ᎢᏯᏓᏛᏁᏗ ᎠᏓᏁᎸᏍᎩ ᎦᏐᎭᎾᎳᎩᏍᏗ ᎠᏔᏲᎯᎭ ᎤᏓᏄᎸᏅᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="RUIM Service Provider unlock request unsuccessful.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>RUIM Service Provider unlock request unsuccessful.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>RUIM ᎢᏯᏓᏛᏁᏗ ᎠᏓᏁᎸᏍᎩ ᎦᏐᎭᎾᎳᎩᏍᏗ ᎠᏔᏲᎯᎭ ᎤᏓᏄᎸᏅᎢ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Finger placement should vary slightly each time. Please try again.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Finger placement should vary slightly each time. Please try again.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎦᏰᏌᏛ ᎤᏙᏢᏒ ᎾᎢᏳᏃ ᏧᏓᎴᎾᎢ ᏍᏗᎩᏓ ᎢᏧᎳ ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒ. ᎰᏩᏊ ᏏᏊ ᏥᎭᏁᎵᏓ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Requesting RUIM service provider unlock\u2026">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Requesting RUIM service provider unlock\u2026</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏥᏔᏲᎯᎲᎢ RUIM ᎢᏯᏓᏛᏁᏗ ᎠᏓᏁᎸᏍᎩ ᎠᏂᏐᎭᎾᎳᎩ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Display refresh rate">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Display refresh rate</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎬᏂᎨᏒ ᏱᎬᏁᏗ ᎠᏤᎲᏍᏙᏓ ᎠᎦᏈᏴᎡᎲᎢ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="SIM Service Provider unlock successful.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>SIM Service Provider unlock successful.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>SIM ᎢᏯᏓᏛᏁᏗ ᎠᏓᏁᎸᏍᎩ ᎠᏂᏐᎭᎾᎳᎩ ᏄᏓᏄᎸᏅᎾ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
