                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Choose photo</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎠᏑᏰᏍᏗ ᏗᏓᏥᎶᏍᏔᏅᎢ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Your PIN can’t be the last 4 digits of your phone number">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Your PIN can’t be the last 4 digits of your phone number</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᏨᎤᎢ PIN ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎨᎡᎩ ᏥᎩ ᎣᏂ 4 ᎠᏎᏍᏗ ᎤᎿ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎠᏎᏍᏗ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Cannot record during a call.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Cannot record during a call.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᏕᎦᏅᏅᏛᎢ ᎾᎯᏳ ᎨᏒ ᏪᏯᎾ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id=" Visual Voicemail:You can play your voicemails in the order of your choice.Your most recent voicemails appear at the top of the list.Premium subscribers have access to voicemail text transcripts. Premium subscribers can alsoreceive voicemails and transcripts of voicemails in their email inbox.Setup:If you’re a first time user, you’ll need to set up your voicemail. This is aneasy 2-step process that involves choosing a PIN and a voicemail greeting. Your default PINis the last 4 digits of your phone number, but you’ll need to change it as part of thesetup.Greetings:You can choose from 3 types of voicemail greetings. These are used to greet your callerswhen they reach your voicemail.Custom Greeting: Allows you to record a personal greetingName Greeting: Allows you to record your nameDefault Greeting: Standard greeting with your phone numberHow to change your PIN and greeting?You can change your PIN and voicemail greeting anytime by going to Settings -&gt;Visual Voicemail.How to see this tutorial later?You can revisit this tutorial anytime by going to Settings &gt; Visual Voicemail.What happens when callers leave a voicemail when you don’t have a data connection?You’ll always be notified when you receive a new voicemail. You can listen to yourvoicemails by tapping the “Voicemail” button in your phone app. Your voicemailswill download automatically when a data connection is restored.Are voicemails downloaded automatically?Voicemails will download automatically when you’re connected to Wi-Fi. Whenyou’re using a mobile network, you can turn on auto download by going toSettings &gt; Visual Voicemail. ">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term> Visual Voicemail:You can play your voicemails in the order of your choice.Your most recent voicemails appear at the top of the list.Premium subscribers have access to voicemail text transcripts. Premium subscribers can alsoreceive voicemails and transcripts of voicemails in their email inbox.Setup:If you’re a first time user, you’ll need to set up your voicemail. This is aneasy 2-step process that involves choosing a PIN and a voicemail greeting. Your default PINis the last 4 digits of your phone number, but you’ll need to change it as part of thesetup.Greetings:You can choose from 3 types of voicemail greetings. These are used to greet your callerswhen they reach your voicemail.Custom Greeting: Allows you to record a personal greetingName Greeting: Allows you to record your nameDefault Greeting: Standard greeting with your phone numberHow to change your PIN and greeting?You can change your PIN and voicemail greeting anytime by going to Settings -&gt;Visual Voicemail.How to see this tutorial later?You can revisit this tutorial anytime by going to Settings &gt; Visual Voicemail.What happens when callers leave a voicemail when you don’t have a data connection?You’ll always be notified when you receive a new voicemail. You can listen to yourvoicemails by tapping the “Voicemail” button in your phone app. Your voicemailswill download automatically when a data connection is restored.Are voicemails downloaded automatically?Voicemails will download automatically when you’re connected to Wi-Fi. Whenyou’re using a mobile network, you can turn on auto download by going toSettings &gt; Visual Voicemail. </term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏓᏟᎶᏍᏛ ᎧᏁᎬ:ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎤᎾᏛᏁᎸᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏓᏅᏍᏗ ᎾᎿ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏑᏰᏍᏗ.ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎤᎪᏗᏗ ᎾᏞᎬ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎬᏂᎨᏒᎢ ᎤᎿ ᏥᎩ ᏩᎦᎸᎳᏗᏴ ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩ ᏕᎦᏅᏛᎢ.ᏫᏓᏤᏢᎢ ᏔᏓᏅᎵ ᎤᎭ ᎠᏴᏍᏗ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎪᏪᎳᏅᎢ ᎬᏂᎨᏒ ᏂᎬᏅ ᎪᏪᎳᏅᎢ. ᏫᏓᏤᏢᎢ ᏔᏓᏅᎵ ᎤᎭ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎾᏍᏊᎦᏁᏍᏗ ᎤᏁᎬ ᏃᎴ ᎬᏂᎨᏒ ᏂᎬᏅ ᎪᏪᎳᏅᎢ ᎾᎿ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎾᎿ ᎤᎾᏤᎵ ᎠᎾᎦᎵᏍᎩ ᎪᏪᎵ ᏂᎬᏅ ᎧᏁᏌᎢ.ᎦᎧᎲᏍᎬᎢ:ᎾᎿ ᏂᎯ ᎨᎡᎩ Ꭰ ᎢᎬᏱ ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒ ᎬᏗᏍᎩ, ᏂᎯ ᎠᏎ ᎤᏚᎸᏓ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎦᎧᎲᏍᎬᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎧᏁᎬ. ᎯᎠ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎠᎠᎯᏗᎨᎢ 2-ᎢᏯᎳᏍᎬᏓ ᎠᏂᎯᎵᏒ ᎥᏍᎩᎾ ᎠᏓᏠᏯᏍᏙᏗ ᎤᏑᏰᎭ Ꭰ PIN ᏃᎴ Ꭰ ᎧᏁᎬ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ. ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏓᏁᏟᏴᏍᏗᏍᎩ PINᎨᎡᎢ ᏥᎩ ᎣᏂ 4 ᎠᏎᏍᏗ ᎾᎿ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎠᏎᏍᏗ, ᎠᏎᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎠᏎ ᎤᏚᎸᏓ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎦᏁᏟᏴᏍᏗ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎤᎿ ᎢᎦᏛᏉ ᎾᎿ ᏥᎩᎦᎧᎲᏍᎬᎢ.ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ:ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᏣᏑᏰᏍᏗ ᏅᏓᏳᏓᎴᏅᎯ 3 ᎢᏧᏍᏗ ᎤᎿ ᎧᏁᎬ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ. ᎯᎠᏃ ᎨᎡᎩ ᎬᏔᏅᎯ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᏓᎵᎮᎵᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎠᏰᎵᏍᎩᎢᏳᏃ ᏧᏄ ᎠᏙᏯᏅᎯᏗᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎧᏁᎬ.ᏄᏍᏛ ᎢᏯᏛᏁᏗ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ: ᏓᎵᏍᎪᎸᏓᏁᎲ ᏂᎯ ᎤᎿᎢ ᏕᎦᏅᏅᏛᎢ Ꭰ ᎤᏩᏌ ᎤᏤᎵ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘᏚᏅᏙᎥ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ: ᏓᎵᏍᎪᎸᏓᏁᎲ ᏂᎯ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏕᎦᏅᏅᏛᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏚᏅᏙᎥᎠᏓᏁᏟᏴᏍᏗᏍᎩ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ: ᎢᎬᏩᏍᏗᎭ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ ᎬᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎠᏎᏍᏗᏰᎵ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎦᏁᏟᏴᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ PIN ᏃᎴ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ?ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎦᏁᏟᏴᏍᏗ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ PIN ᏃᎴ ᎧᏁᎬ ᎠᎵᎮᎵᏤᏘ ᎢᎸᎯᏳ ᎬᏗ ᏓᏰᏏ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ -&gt;ᏓᏟᎶᏍᏛ ᎧᏁᎬ.ᏰᎵ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᎪᏩᏛᏗ ᎯᎠ ᎠᏕᎶᏆᏍᏙᏗ ᎣᏂᏯᎨᏍᏗ?ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎠᎪᎵᏰᏗ ᎯᎠ ᎠᏕᎶᏆᏍᏙᏗ ᎢᎸᎯᏳ ᎬᏗ ᏓᏰᏏ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ &gt; ᏓᏟᎶᏍᏛ ᎧᏁᎬ.ᎦᏙ ᏂᏚᎵᏍᏔᏅ ᎢᏳᏃ ᎠᏰᎵᏍᎩ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᏗ Ꭰ ᎧᏁᎬ ᎢᏳᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎤᎭ Ꭰ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ?ᏂᎯ ᎠᏎ ᏂᎪᎯᎸᎢ ᎨᏒᎩ ᎠᏓᏃᎯᏎᏗ ᎢᏳᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎦᏁᏍᏗ Ꭰ ᏗᏤ ᎧᏁᎬ. ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎭᏛᏓᏍᏓ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏂᏨᎤᎢᎧᏁᎬ ᎬᏗ ᎤᏟᏍᏓ ᎭᏐᏅᏍᏓ ᏥᎩ “ᎧᏁᎬ” ᎦᏛᏗ ᎾᎿ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏗᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᎬᏙᏗ. ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎧᏁᎬᎠᏎ ᎡᎳᏗᏟ ᎦᏢᏍᎬᎢ ᎤᏩᏌᏊ ᏱᎬᏁᎯ ᎢᏳᏃ Ꭰ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎨᎡᎢ ᎪᏢᎯᏌᏅ.ᎨᎡᎩ ᎤᏁᎬ ᎡᎳᏗᎬᏘ ᏫᎦᏢᏅᎯ ᎤᏩᏌᏊ ᏱᎬᏁᎯ?ᎤᏁᎬ ᎠᏎ ᎡᎳᏗᏟ ᎦᏢᏍᎬᎢ ᎤᏩᏌᏊ ᏱᎬᏁᎯ ᎢᏳᏃ ᏂᎯ ᎨᎡᎩ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎾᎿᎢ Wi-Fi. ᎢᏳᏃᏂᎯ ᎨᎡᎩ ᎬᏗᎭ Ꭰ ᎠᏂᎩᏍᎩ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ, ᏂᎯ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎯᏍᏚᎢ ᎤᏩᏌᏊ ᏱᎬᏁᎯ ᎡᎳᏗᏟ ᎦᏢᏍᎬᎢ ᎬᏗ ᏓᏰᏏ ᎾᎿᎢᏕᎦᎧᎲᎢ &gt; ᏓᏟᎶᏍᏛ ᎧᏁᎬ. </term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Your PIN can’t have more than 2 repeated numbers (such as 1222, 3331)">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Your PIN can’t have more than 2 repeated numbers (such as 1222, 3331)</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᏨᎤᎢ PIN ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎤᎭ ᎤᎪᏗᏊ ᎡᏍᎦᏉ 2 ᎤᏩᏘᎶᏓ ᏗᏎᏍᏗ (ᏕᎧᏁᎢᏍᏔᏅᎯ 1222, 3331)</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Your PIN can’t have more than 2 consecutive numbers (such as 1235, 4561, 5321)">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Your PIN can’t have more than 2 consecutive numbers (such as 1235, 4561, 5321)</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᏨᎤᎢ PIN ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎤᎭ ᎤᎪᏗᏊ ᎡᏍᎦᏉ 2 ᏂᎪᎯᎸᎢ ᏗᏎᏍᏗ (ᏕᎧᏁᎢᏍᏔᏅᎯ 1235, 4561, 5321)</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Need to talk to you about tomorrow's meeting!">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Need to talk to you about tomorrow's meeting!</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎤᏚᎸᏓ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏍᏓᏟᏃᎮᏗ ᏂᎯ ᎢᎸᏨ ᏑᎾᎴ ᏓᎾᏠᏍᎬᎢ!</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Real Time Text (RTT) allows you to have a text conversation during a call.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Real Time Text (RTT) allows you to have a text conversation during a call.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎤᏙᎯᏳ ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒ ᎪᏪᎳᏅᎢ (RTT) ᏓᎵᏍᎪᎸᏓᏁᎲ ᏂᎯ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎤᎭ Ꭰ ᎪᏪᎳᏅᎢ ᎠᎾᏟᏃᎮᏍᎬᎢ ᎾᎯᏳ Ꭰ ᏪᏴᎾ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Learn more">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Learn more</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎤᏥ ᎢᎦᎢ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Not now">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Not now</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎭᏗ ᏆᏊ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Call is transferring to the cellular network. Voice and data rates may apply.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Call is transferring to the cellular network. Voice and data rates may apply.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏪᏯᎾ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏙᏓᏰᏣᏲᎯᏎᎵ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏥᎩ ᏫᏚᏍᏗᎬᎢ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ. ᎤᏁᎬ ᏃᎴ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᏗᎪᏣᎴᏒᏛ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎲᏓ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Can't connect video call">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Can't connect video call</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏪᏯᎾ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="You cannot make a call while the device is in airplane mode. Would you like to turn airplane mode off?">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>You cannot make a call while the device is in airplane mode. Would you like to turn airplane mode off?</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏂᎯ ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᎪᏒᏗ Ꭰ ᏪᏯᎾ ᎾᎯᏳᎢ ᏥᎩ ᏥᏂᎬᏅᏗᏓᎾ ᎨᎡᎩ ᎾᎿ ᏥᏳ ᏄᏍᏛᎢ . ᏯᏓᎯᏗᏏ ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᎯᎸᏉᏗ ᎾᎿᎢ ᎠᎦᏔᎲᏍᏗ ᏥᏳ ᏄᏍᏛᎢ ᎠᏍᏚᎭ?</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Wi-Fi no longer available. Your call is transferring to the cellular network. Voice and data rates may apply.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Wi-Fi no longer available. Your call is transferring to the cellular network. Voice and data rates may apply.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>Wi-Fi ᎭᏗ ᎦᏅᎯᏓᎨ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ. ᏂᏨᎤᎢ ᏪᏯᎾ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏙᏓᏰᏣᏲᎯᏎᎵ ᎾᎿᎢ ᏥᎩ ᏫᏚᏍᏗᎬᎢ ᎫᏓᎸᎢ. ᎤᏁᎬ ᏃᎴ ᎦᏘᏍᎩᏌᏅᎯ ᏗᎪᏣᎴᏒᏛ ᏰᎵᏯ ᎲᏓ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Simultaneous voice and real-time text calling is currently available only over high speed LTE and Wi-Fi networks.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Simultaneous voice and real-time text calling is currently available only over high speed LTE and Wi-Fi networks.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎡᏧᎳᎭ ᏂᎦᎵᏍᏗᏍᎬ ᎪᎱᏍᏗ ᎤᏁᎬ ᏃᎴ ᎤᏙᎯᏳ ᎠᏥᎢᎵᏒᎢ ᎪᏪᎳᏅᎢ ᎠᏓᏴᎳᏛᏍᎩ ᏓᏯᏂᏍᎬ ᎨᎡᎢ ᏃᏊ ᏥᎩ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ ᎤᏅᏒ ᎢᏴᏛ ᎦᎸᎳᏗ ᎠᏍᎦᏃᎳ LTE ᏃᎴ Wi-Fi ᏚᎾᏚᏓᎵ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Can't merge audio only calls with video calls.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Can't merge audio only calls with video calls.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᎨᏍᏗ ᏰᎵ ᏓᏠᎯᏍᏛ ᎤᏃᏴᎬ ᎤᏅᏒ ᏓᏯᏂ ᎬᏗ ᎤᏁᎬ ᏓᏯᏂ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="Based on your activity">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>Based on your activity</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>ᏓᎳᏏᏔᏅᎩ ᎾᏍᎩ ᏥᎾᏛᏁᎲ</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
            <termEntry id="RTT is not available for this 911 call.">
                <langSet xml:lang="en-US"><tig><term>RTT is not available for this 911 call.</term></tig></langSet>
                <langSet xml:lang="chr"><tig><term>RTT ᎭᏗ ᎠᏛᏅᎢᏍᏔᏅ ᎤᎬᏩᏟ ᎯᎠ 911 ᏪᏯᎾ.</term></tig></langSet>
            </termEntry>
